    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is another continuation of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3523568981\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41569\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41569/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41569\">#41569</a>. In that PR, I rebranded two guides: Selection and traversal, and Building and updating, which are incredibly thin and outdated, with the promise to update them to make them cover the full DOM spec. Here is the first part, which touches the Selection and traversal guide.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45646",
            "title": "Modernize DOM guide (4): complete the Selection and traversal guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T21:04:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T21:02:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/292674468?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrects the single-select tree guidance so <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-selected</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> on the selected tree item, <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> on other selectable tree items, and omitted only from tree items that are not selectable.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous wording told readers to omit <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-selected</code> from every unselected item. That made it difficult for assistive technologies to distinguish an unselected selectable item from an item that cannot be selected.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Validated with the target-page MarkdownLint, Prettier, front-matter, and file-check scripts under Node 24.21.0 and npm 11.19.0.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41378.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3478927005\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41378\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41378/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41378\">#41378</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45645",
            "title": "Clarify aria-selected states for single-select trees",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T20:13:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T20:13:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "JalenBuildsHub",
                "url": "https://github.com/JalenBuildsHub"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Writes leftover destination cases as `log into`, matching <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5282879013\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45382\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45382/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45382\">#45382</a> and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5426771760\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45633\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45633/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45633\">#45633</a>.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Server-side introduction: \"Log in to your account\" → \"Log into your account\"</li>\n<li>`aria-expanded` example help text: \"log in to this service\" → \"log into this service\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Noun uses such as the login page are left alone.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5282879013\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45382\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45382/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45382\">#45382</a> established that `login` is the noun, `log in` is the verb, and a destination is written `log into`. These two leftovers were missed.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45644",
            "title": "Use leftover log into when the verb has a destination",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T19:02:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T19:00:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the missing preposition `to` after `grant permission` on two leftover Permissions-Policy notes.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>`Element.requestFullscreen()`</li>\n<li>Screen Wake Lock API</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Both currently say \"grant permission a particular third-party origin\". The Geolocation API note already has \"grant permission to a particular third-party origin\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The verb `grant permission` takes `to` before the recipient. These two sentences were missed when <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5426778468\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45635\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45635/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45635\">#45635</a> hyphenated the leftover `third-party` modifiers in the same notes.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45643",
            "title": "Add missing to after grant permission",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T19:02:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T19:00:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hyphenates leftover `server-side` modifiers in two places.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Private State Token API: \"server side application\"</li>\n<li>CycleTracker secure connection: \"local server side language\" (the hash already uses `server-side`)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Predicative uses such as \"on the server side\", and \"Server Side Rendering (SSR)\", are left alone.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5323451413\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45462\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45462/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45462\">#45462</a> already hyphenated `client-side` when it modifies a following noun. These are the same leftover on the server-side side of that pair.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45641",
            "title": "Hyphenate leftover server-side modifiers",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T18:43:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T18:41:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hyphenates leftover `case-insensitive` modifiers when they precede a noun.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>HSTS: \"a case insensitive match\"</li>\n<li>URN: \"a case insensitive identifier\"</li>\n<li>EXSLT `regexp:match`, `regexp:replace`, and `regexp:test`: \"Case insensitive match\" / \"case insensitive fashion\"</li>\n<li>Django models example: \"Genre already exists (case insensitive match)\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also drops a stray `&lt;` after \"match\" on the `regexp:test` page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Predicative uses such as \"this property is case insensitive\" are left alone.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Used before a noun this is a compound modifier and takes a hyphen, matching the same leftover pattern as <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5323451413\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45462\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45462/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45462\">#45462</a>. The same Django models page already writes \"case-insensitive exact match\".</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45640",
            "title": "Hyphenate leftover case-insensitive modifiers",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T18:42:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T18:41:01.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF156 adds support for the async Clipboard API to use web custom formats.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The  API allows you to create a <code class=\"notranslate\">ClipboardItem</code> that contains several representations of a copied object, such as version in HTML and Text, and push it to the system clipboard. Something else can read the clipboard and get back tha object - then choose the best format it understands.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The update allows you to (behind a pref) use other types than PNG, HTML, txt.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What this update does is make the model above clear, because it wasn't - it referred too much to \"arbitrary types\" can didn't capture \"different representations\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the first part of the job. After this I'll do the custom web formats bit.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5312307167\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45430/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430\">#45430</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45620",
            "title": "FF156 ClipBoard Async API - clarify types",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T15:16:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T07:07:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43131.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3941254411\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43131\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43131/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43131\">#43131</a>. Note that Firefox seems to behave differently but not sure if it merits a note.</p>",
