        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #22588.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1466998757\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/22588\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/22588/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/22588\">#22588</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">According to BCD, FF 149+ supports <code class=\"notranslate\">console.timeStamp()</code> to the profiler, so this content isn't \"wrong\" per se, but certainly not future-proof. Replaced with handwavy claims that it's implementation dependent, because there's BCD anyway.</p>",
